<SECTION image-layout="right" background-color="#1a1a1a">
  <IMG class="accent-image" query="Jigar Shah speaking at clean energy conference, professional headshot, authoritative pose, dark background with green accent lighting">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">The Commercial Inflection Point Has Arrived</SPAN></H1>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV data-vertical-align="start">
        <BLOCKQUOTE><P><SPAN text-color="#00D4AA"><I>"We're witnessing the fastest technology cost decline in industrial history. Solar, wind, batteries, and hydrogen are all following exponential improvement curves that make fossil fuels economically obsolete within this decade. The question is no longer if these technologies will dominate, but how quickly capital markets will recognize the transition and redeploy accordingly."</I></SPAN></P></BLOCKQUOTE>
      </DIV>
      <DIV data-vertical-align="start">
        <P><B><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">— Jigar Shah, Director of the U.S. Department of Energy Loan Programs Office</SPAN></B></P>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Shah oversees <SPAN text-color="#00D4AA">$400 billion</SPAN> in federal loan authority for clean energy deployment and previously founded SunEdison, which pioneered solar power purchase agreements. His assessment carries significant weight given his dual perspective as both a successful clean energy entrepreneur and the federal official responsible for the largest clean energy financing program in U.S. history.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>